---
title: Pressure-Cooker Beef Osso Buco
servings: 2
prepTime: 45 min
cookTime: 50 min
Rating: 10/10
Description: Meat is super tender. Pair with French bread or serve it over polenta, mashed potatoes or pasta. This dish reheats well, so you can make ahead.
source: https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/pressure-cooker-beef-osso-bucco/
tags: Alcohol, Beef, Pressure Cooker
---

= Preparation =
In a large shallow dish, combine @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}, @salt{1/2%teaspoon}, and @pepper{1/2%teaspoon}.
Pat @beef shanks{2}(14 ounces each) dry with paper towels.
Add beef to dish, 1 piece at a time; turn to coat.

= Pressure Cooking =
Select saute setting on a 6-qt. electric #pressure cooker{} and adjust for medium heat.
Add @butter{1%tbsp} and @olive oil{1%tbsp}; brown 3 beef shanks.

Remove from pressure cooker; add @white wine{3%tbsp}(or beef broth), stirring to loosen browned bits. 

In a large bowl, combine @diced tomatoes{7%oz}(undrained), @beef broth{1/2%cup}, @carrot{1}(chopped),
@onion{1/2}(medium), @celery{1/2%rib}(sliced), @dried thyme{1/2%tsp}, @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}, and @bay leaf{1}. 
Return browned beef shanks to cooker; pour in the tomato mixture.

Lock lid; close pressure-release valve. Adjust to pressure-cook on high for ~{40%minutes}.
Allow pressure to naturally release for ~{10%minutes}, then quick-release any remaining pressure.
Remove meat and vegetables from pressure cooker; keep warm. 

> Do not overfill the pressure cooker.
> If making more than about 3 shanks, cook the first batch and set aside after cooking,
> and repeat the Cooking stage for the remaining servings.

= Finishing Sauce =
After removing all meat and vegetables, discard bay leaves. 
Skim fat from cooking juices. Select saute setting and adjust for medium heat. 
Bring to a boil. 

In a small bowl, mix @cornstarch{1%tbsp} and @water{2%tbsp}(cold) until smooth; stir into cooking juices.
Return to a boil, stirring constantly; cook and stir until thickened, about ~{2%minutes}. Press cancel.

= Serving =
In a small bowl, combine @parsley{1/3%cup}(fresh, minced), @lemon zest{1%tsp}(fresh grated),
@orange zest{1%tsp}(fresh grated), and @garlic cloves{2}(minced).

Serve beef with gremolata and sauce.

= Nutritional Information (per serving) =
398 calories, 15g fat, 6g saturated fat, 112mg cholesterol, 640mg sodium, 17g carbohydrate, 5g sugars, 4g fiber, 47g protein
